    "content": {
      "value": "<p>This page documents the alternative catalogue sync design using <strong>SCAPI Admin APIs</strong> instead of WebDAV file-based import. It covers the same three data domains — Product, Price, and Inventory — and follows the same section structure as the file-based design for direct comparison.</p><blockquote><p><strong>Context:</strong> The file-based design (WebDAV + import job) is the recommended approach for Zimmermann's catalogue scale. This SCAPI Admin API design is documented as the alternative pattern — applicable for real-time single-product event scenarios or if the file-based approach is ruled out. See the <a href=\"https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/312508418\">parent page comparison</a> for the full pro/con trade-off.</p></blockquote><p>Related pages: - <a href=\"https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/312508418\">TSD: Catalogue Sync — Product, Price &amp; Inventory (MuleSoft → SFCC)</a> — file-based design - <a href=\"https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/292061208\">TSD: Product — SFCC Catalogue &amp; Data Integration</a> - <a href=\"https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/312377345\">TSD: Product — SFCC Product Attributes</a> - <a href=\"https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/292388871\">TSD: Price — SFCC Pricebooks &amp; Global-e</a></p><hr/><h2><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"aedb951a-df4d-456d-82ec-b85b6c7ee18f\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">1-overview</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>1. Overview</h2><p>In the SCAPI Admin API pattern, MuleSoft calls SFCC REST endpoints directly per product or inventory record. Each domain uses a dedicated SCAPI Admin API family.</p><blockquote><p><strong>API Note:</strong> OCAPI is deprecated. All SFCC Admin API calls use <strong>SCAPI Admin APIs</strong> authenticated via <strong>Account Manager OAuth2 (AmOAuth2)</strong> — client credentials grant.</p><p>⚠️ <strong>Price sync exception:</strong> There is no published SCAPI Admin API or verified OCAPI endpoint for writing pricebook entries programmatically. <strong>Price sync must always use the file-based pricebook XML import</strong> (WebDAV + <code>sfcc-site-archive-import</code> job) regardless of which pattern is chosen for products and inventory. See Section 5.</p></blockquote><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Mechanism</th><th>SCAPI API</th><th>Auth</th><th>API Reference</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Product</td><td>SCAPI Admin API (per product/variant)</td><td>Products Admin API — <code>POST</code> / <code>PUT</code></td><td>AmOAuth2</td><td><a href=\"https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/commerce/commerce-api/references/products\">Products</a></td></tr><tr><td>Price</td><td><strong>File-based only</strong> — WebDAV + import job</td><td>No SCAPI API exists</td><td>AmOAuth2 (WebDAV)</td><td>—</td></tr><tr><td>Inventory</td><td>SCAPI Admin API (per record)</td><td>Inventory Lists API — <code>PUT</code> / <code>PATCH</code></td><td>AmOAuth2</td><td><a href=\"https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/commerce/commerce-api/references/inventory-lists\">Inventory Lists</a></td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>SCAPI Admin API base URL:</strong><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"7857fb83-176b-416e-983b-1dd56b8ff8c0\" ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"theme\">Default</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"language\">none</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[https://{shortCode}.api.commercecloud.salesforce.com]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro></p><p><strong>Auth token acquisition (product and inventory domains):</strong><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"ff162118-ea36-4638-905a-3b021a61c4f0\" ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"theme\">Default</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"language\">none</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[POST https://account.demandware.com/dwsso/oauth2/access_token\nContent-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded\n\ngrant_type=client_credentials\n&client_id={mulesoftClientId}\n&client_secret={mulesoftClientSecret}]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro></p><hr/><h2><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"2ce0e1e8-fe8d-4307-ae9d-5a5f5d44feb1\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">2-sequencing-constraints</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>2. Sequencing Constraints</h2><p>Unlike the file-based import job which handles sequencing internally, the SCAPI Admin API pattern requires MuleSoft to enforce strict operation order across product and inventory domains. Price sync runs independently via file-based import and does not participate in this sequence.</p><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"b5e2e4b9-5ddc-4f63-b0e1-f30d4144af26\" ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"theme\">Default</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"language\">none</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[For each style (master product):\n\n  STEP 1 — Create or update MASTER product\n           POST /product/v1/.../products/{catalogId}\n\n  STEP 2 — Create or update each VARIANT\n           POST /product/v1/.../products/{catalogId}\n           ⚠ Must complete after Step 1 — variant fails if master does not exist\n\n  STEP 3 — Assign products to CATEGORIES\n           PUT /product/v1/.../categories/{categoryId}/products/{productId}\n           ⚠ Must complete after Step 1\n\n  STEP 4 — Write INVENTORY\n           PUT /inventory/v1/.../inventory-lists/{listId}/product-inventory-records/{productId}\n           ⚠ Must complete after Step 2 — variant must exist before inventory record\n\n  STEP 5 — PRICE SYNC (file-based — independent of above sequence)\n           Pricebook XML → WebDAV → sfcc-site-archive-import job\n           Runs on its own schedule\n           ⚠ Variant must exist in SFCC before a pricebook entry for it is valid]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro><hr/><h2><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"752f725e-a44e-4035-b297-d93a53d9a394\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">3-sync-orchestration--mulesoft-flow-product-and-inventory</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>3. Sync Orchestration — MuleSoft Flow (Product and Inventory)</h2><p>The SCAPI Admin API pattern requires a <strong>separate MuleSoft flow per domain</strong> (product, inventory), each with its own retry logic, error tracking, and partial-success handling. Price sync uses the file-based flow documented in the <a href=\"https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/312508418\">parent page</a>.</p><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"3daaecbd-302d-4fc0-a36e-c0f5160fb08c\" ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"theme\">Default</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"language\">none</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[AP21 / NewStore (source event or scheduler trigger)\n  │\n  ▼\nMuleSoft\n  │\n  ├── 1. GET AmOAuth2 TOKEN\n  │   POST https://account.demandware.com/dwsso/oauth2/access_token\n  │   Cache token; refresh before expiry (typically 30 min TTL)\n  │\n  ├── 2. CHECK PRODUCT EXISTS (product domain only)\n  │   GET /product/v1/.../products/{catalogId}/{productId}\n  │   → 200: product exists → use PUT to update\n  │   → 404: product does not exist → use POST to create\n  │\n  ├── 3. EXECUTE API CALL\n  │   POST / PUT per domain (see Sections 4 and 6)\n  │   Headers: Authorization: Bearer {amOAuth2Token}\n  │            Content-Type: application/json\n  │   → 200 / 201: success\n  │   → 4xx: business error — log, skip record, continue\n  │   → 429: rate limit — back off and retry\n  │   → 5xx: server error — retry up to 3 times with exponential back-off\n  │\n  ├── 4. TRACK RESULT PER RECORD\n  │   { productId: \"success\" | \"failed\" | \"skipped\" }\n  │\n  ├── 5. CONTINUE TO NEXT RECORD\n  │   Do not abort entire batch on a single record failure\n  │\n  └── 6. POST-RUN SUMMARY\n        If any records failed → raise alert via Anypoint monitoring\n        Store failed record IDs for manual replay or next-run retry]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro><hr/><h2><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"fe53642e-1d39-4b51-a19f-d4d0e3b7409e\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">4-product-sync</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>4. Product Sync</h2><h3><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"9806c401-b1b8-44a5-8e80-a643d9e88553\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">41-trigger</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>4.1 Trigger</h3><p>AP21 product create or update event consumed by MuleSoft. Can be event-driven (real-time per product) or scheduled batch.</p><h3><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"4fe0d75e-7d6d-40fa-8252-fc451462c9da\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">42-api-endpoints</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>4.2 API Endpoints</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>When</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Create master</td><td><code>POST</code></td><td><code>/product/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/products/{catalogId}</code></td><td>Product does not exist</td></tr><tr><td>Update master</td><td><code>PUT</code></td><td><code>/product/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/products/{catalogId}/{productId}</code></td><td>Product exists</td></tr><tr><td>Create variant</td><td><code>POST</code></td><td><code>/product/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/products/{catalogId}</code></td><td>Variant does not exist — after master created</td></tr><tr><td>Update variant</td><td><code>PUT</code></td><td><code>/product/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/products/{catalogId}/{productId}</code></td><td>Variant exists</td></tr><tr><td>Assign to category</td><td><code>PUT</code></td><td><code>/product/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/categories/{categoryId}/products/{productId}</code></td><td>After product created</td></tr></tbody></table><h3><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"45739ff7-c5de-4c1b-801d-6f1daf531256\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">43-master-product-payload</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>4.3 Master Product Payload</h3><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"779dae86-fc29-41fe-b382-fbaa140001e2\" ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"theme\">Default</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"language\">json</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[{\n  \"id\": \"4673TS251\",\n  \"name\": { \"default\": \"Aster Fit & Flare Dress\" },\n  \"longDescription\": { \"default\": \"...\" },\n  \"online\": true,\n  \"searchable\": true,\n  \"taxClassId\": \"standard\",\n  \"type\": { \"master\": true },\n  \"variationAttributes\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"color\",\n      \"name\": { \"default\": \"Colour\" },\n      \"values\": [{ \"value\": \"GVSCP\", \"name\": { \"default\": \"Guava Seascape\" } }]\n    },\n    { \"id\": \"size\", \"name\": { \"default\": \"Size\" } }\n  ],\n  \"c_styleNumber\": \"4673TS251\",\n  \"c_season\": \"SS25\",\n  \"c_label\": \"Ready to Wear\",\n  \"c_fabricComposition\": \"100% Silk\",\n  \"c_careInstructions\": \"Dry clean only\",\n  \"c_countryOfOrigin\": \"China\",\n  \"c_isFinalSale\": false\n}]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro><h3><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"6dde61aa-3909-4d0f-8750-fbcd74d3c4b8\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">44-variant-product-payload</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>4.4 Variant Product Payload</h3><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"8ca8510e-d093-4771-948f-4f8ea220e692\" ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"theme\">Default</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"language\">json</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[{\n  \"id\": \"4673TS251GVSCP0P\",\n  \"masterProductId\": \"4673TS251\",\n  \"upc\": \"9312345678901\",\n  \"online\": true,\n  \"searchable\": false,\n  \"type\": { \"variant\": true },\n  \"variationValues\": { \"color\": \"GVSCP\", \"size\": \"0P\" },\n  \"c_color\": \"GVSCP\",\n  \"c_refinementColor\": \"Guava Seascape\",\n  \"c_size\": \"0P\"\n}]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro><h3><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"26a18144-392e-460e-ba02-ed0d61400705\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">45-upsert-pattern</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>4.5 Upsert Pattern</h3><p>SCAPI does not have a native upsert endpoint for products. MuleSoft must check existence before every write:</p><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"ef7106a1-ec04-4bce-9d21-6f9f7fcbbd83\" ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"theme\">Default</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"language\">none</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[GET /product/v1/.../products/{catalogId}/{productId}\n  → 200 → PUT (update)\n  → 404 → POST (create)]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro><p>For a batch of 1,000 products × 5 variants = 12,000 API calls (6,000 existence checks + 6,000 writes).</p><hr/><h2><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"4da67ee3-0c59-46b7-a7e9-1482d202cc61\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">5-price-sync--filebased-only</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>5. Price Sync — File-Based Only</h2><blockquote><p>⚠️ <strong>No SCAPI Admin API exists for writing pricebook entries.</strong></p><p>This has been confirmed against Salesforce developer documentation — no SCAPI Admin API for pricebook entry writes exists as a published endpoint. OCAPI is deprecated and must not be used for new integrations.</p><p><strong>Price sync must use the file-based pricebook XML import regardless of which pattern is chosen for products and inventory.</strong></p></blockquote><h3><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"893ae6e9-8963-4906-93ef-3e7288ec4181\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">51-mechanism</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>5.1 Mechanism</h3><p>Pricebook XML delivered via WebDAV + <code>sfcc-site-archive-import</code> job — identical to the file-based design. See <a href=\"https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/312508418\">TSD: Catalogue Sync — Product, Price &amp; Inventory — Section 5</a> for the full specification.</p><h3><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"2603e71a-c4c9-4650-97c5-b701505e7a00\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">52-scope</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>5.2 Scope</h3><p>Domestic sites only — AU, UK, US, EU. International sites (USIntl, EUIntl, HK, ME) pricing is managed by Global-e.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Site</th><th>List Pricebook ID</th><th>Sale Pricebook ID</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>ZimmermannAU</td><td><code>au-aud-list-prices</code></td><td><code>au-aud-sale-prices</code></td></tr><tr><td>ZimmermannUK</td><td><code>uk-gbp-list-prices</code></td><td><code>uk-gbp-sale-prices</code></td></tr><tr><td>ZimmermannUS</td><td><code>us-usd-list-prices</code></td><td><code>us-usd-sale-prices</code></td></tr><tr><td>ZimmermannEU</td><td><code>eu-eur-list-prices</code></td><td><code>eu-eur-sale-prices</code></td></tr></tbody></table><h3><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"5c5aa025-65ce-4bea-8b33-3845aa6ae57a\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">53-implication-for-hybrid-pattern</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>5.3 Implication for Hybrid Pattern</h3><p>If Zimmermann selects SCAPI Admin API for product and inventory sync, MuleSoft must still implement the WebDAV + job-trigger flow for price sync. Both flows co-exist:</p><ul><li><strong>Product + Inventory</strong> → SCAPI Admin API per-record calls</li><li><strong>Price</strong> → WebDAV pricebook XML + <code>sfcc-site-archive-import</code> job</li></ul><hr/><h2><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"dc3641c1-006a-412f-a779-a48f9b50a264\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">6-inventory-sync</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>6. Inventory Sync</h2><h3><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"a85499c1-5007-4e81-a301-b41ed761a6b7\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">61-trigger</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>6.1 Trigger</h3><p>Every 15 minutes per region (AU, GB, US). EU, EUIntl, HK, ME coverage to be confirmed — see open item #3.</p><h3><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"c1bbeacd-8945-4d0e-993a-71a0fbaacc38\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">62-source</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>6.2 Source</h3><p>NewStore S3 availability export → MuleSoft decompresses and transforms to SCAPI Inventory Lists API payloads.</p><h3><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"89d80d94-e3a4-4cec-8ae1-536ce15530bf\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">63-api-reference</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>6.3 API Reference</h3><p><a href=\"https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/commerce/commerce-api/references/inventory-lists\">SCAPI Inventory Lists API</a> — Admin API, AmOAuth2 auth.</p><p><strong>Base path:</strong><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"c6e32d1b-27ed-453d-af9e-03dade422822\" ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"theme\">Default</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"language\">none</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[https://{shortCode}.api.commercecloud.salesforce.com\n/inventory/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/inventory-lists/{listId}]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro></p><p><strong>Required scope:</strong><code>sfcc.inventory.availability.rw</code></p><h3><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"35ddce99-fa56-44bf-bc87-eca4ba710c02\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">64-api-endpoints</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>6.4 API Endpoints</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th>Method</th><th>Endpoint</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Create or update inventory record</td><td><code>PUT</code></td><td><code>/inventory/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/inventory-lists/{listId}/product-inventory-records/{productId}</code></td><td>Full replace of record</td></tr><tr><td>Partial update inventory record</td><td><code>PATCH</code></td><td><code>/inventory/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/inventory-lists/{listId}/product-inventory-records/{productId}</code></td><td>Update specific fields only. Negative allocation amounts are disallowed</td></tr><tr><td>Get inventory record</td><td><code>GET</code></td><td><code>/inventory/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/inventory-lists/{listId}/product-inventory-records/{productId}</code></td><td>Read current record before update if needed</td></tr><tr><td>Delete inventory record</td><td><code>DELETE</code></td><td><code>/inventory/v1/organizations/{organizationId}/inventory-lists/{listId}/product-inventory-records/{productId}</code></td><td>Remove record entirely</td></tr></tbody></table><h3><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"2a6059fd-ab0a-4189-80ff-5e8b2943dee5\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">65-inventory-record-payload</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>6.5 Inventory Record Payload</h3><p><code>PUT</code> — full record write:</p><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"8ec41787-1551-4c95-831b-70a08b7c61db\" ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"theme\">Default</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"language\">json</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[{\n  \"allocation\": 12,\n  \"allocationResetDate\": \"2025-07-09T00:00:00.000Z\",\n  \"ats\": 12,\n  \"onOrder\": 0,\n  \"perpetual\": false,\n  \"preorderable\": false,\n  \"preorderAllocation\": 0,\n  \"backorderable\": false,\n  \"backorderAllocation\": 0,\n  \"stockLevel\": 12\n}]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro><p><code>PATCH</code> — partial update (quantity only):</p><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"d6e1305c-a7cc-4ae0-a65a-2592b0cc986b\" ac:name=\"code\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"theme\">Default</ac:parameter><ac:parameter ac:name=\"language\">json</ac:parameter><ac:plain-text-body><![CDATA[{\n  \"allocation\": 8,\n  \"ats\": 8,\n  \"stockLevel\": 8\n}]]></ac:plain-text-body></ac:structured-macro><blockquote><p><strong>Note:</strong> Negative allocation amounts are explicitly disallowed by the SCAPI Inventory Lists API — MuleSoft must validate that no negative values are sent.</p></blockquote><h3><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"f786f24e-69fe-4dc0-b29b-244a12a48c0e\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">66-persite-inventory-lists</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>6.6 Per-Site Inventory Lists</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Site</th><th>Inventory List ID</th><th>Sync Region</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>ZimmermannAU</td><td><code>inventory_m_au</code></td><td>AU</td></tr><tr><td>ZimmermannUK</td><td><code>inventory_m_uk</code></td><td>GB</td></tr><tr><td>ZimmermannUS</td><td><code>inventory_m_us</code></td><td>US</td></tr><tr><td>ZimmermannUSIntl</td><td><code>inventory_m_us</code></td><td>US (shared pool)</td></tr><tr><td>ZimmermannEU</td><td><code>inventory_m_eu</code></td><td>TBC</td></tr><tr><td>ZimmermannEUIntl</td><td><code>inventory_m_eu_intl</code></td><td>TBC</td></tr><tr><td>ZimmermannHK</td><td><code>inventory_m_hk</code></td><td>TBC</td></tr><tr><td>ZimmermannME</td><td><code>inventory_m_me</code></td><td>TBC</td></tr></tbody></table><h3><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"70549da5-2647-427b-92e9-d95636dea772\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">67-put-vs-patch</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>6.7 PUT vs PATCH</h3><p>Use <code>PUT</code> for a full inventory record write from NewStore (all fields known). Use <code>PATCH</code> only for targeted partial corrections (e.g. adjusting <code>allocation</code> only after a manual stock adjustment). For the standard 15-minute NewStore sync, <code>PUT</code> is the correct method.</p><hr/><h2><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"7fb495a5-8eec-449b-b86b-e17bda608010\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">7-rate-limits-and-throttling</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>7. Rate Limits and Throttling</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Concern</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Rate limit</td><td>SCAPI Admin API: requests per minute per client — confirm exact limit with Salesforce TAM</td></tr><tr><td>Timeout</td><td>SCAPI Admin API: 60-second response timeout per call</td></tr><tr><td>429 response</td><td>Back off — exponential back-off starting at 5 seconds; retry</td></tr><tr><td>Parallel calls</td><td>Parallelise per domain within rate limit — use Anypoint throttling policy</td></tr><tr><td>Bulk endpoint</td><td>No native bulk endpoint for products or inventory records — each is a separate call</td></tr><tr><td>Recommended rate</td><td>10 requests/second via Anypoint rate limiting; monitor 429 responses in Anypoint</td></tr></tbody></table><hr/><h2><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"208da9fb-4a91-4763-be7b-1fec27dbb0f6\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">8-error-handling</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>8. Error Handling</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Handling</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>404 on product existence check</td><td>Product does not exist — switch to POST. Not an error</td></tr><tr><td>400 Bad Request</td><td>Invalid payload — log record ID and error detail; skip; continue; alert on post-run summary</td></tr><tr><td>409 Conflict</td><td>Concurrent write conflict — retry once after 2-second delay</td></tr><tr><td>422 Unprocessable Entity</td><td>Business validation failure (e.g. master missing for variant, negative inventory) — log and skip</td></tr><tr><td>429 Rate Limited</td><td>Exponential back-off: 5s, 10s, 20s; alert if persistent</td></tr><tr><td>500 / 503 Server Error</td><td>Retry up to 3 times; move to failed queue; alert</td></tr><tr><td>Token expired</td><td>Re-acquire AmOAuth2 token mid-batch; cache and refresh proactively before TTL</td></tr><tr><td>Negative inventory value</td><td>MuleSoft must validate and reject before calling API — negative allocations are disallowed</td></tr><tr><td>Partial batch failure</td><td>Log all failed record IDs; raise Anypoint alert; store for replay</td></tr></tbody></table><hr/><h2><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"2f995d3a-06fd-4086-876b-19069a13996b\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">9-operational-comparison-vs-filebased</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>9. Operational Comparison vs File-Based</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Aspect</th><th>File-Based (WebDAV + Import Job)</th><th>SCAPI Admin API</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bulk catalogue load</td><td>✅ Single zip</td><td>❌ Thousands of calls</td></tr><tr><td>Real-time single product</td><td>❌ Minutes latency</td><td>✅ Seconds</td></tr><tr><td>Rate limits</td><td>✅ None on import job</td><td>❌ Rate limited</td></tr><tr><td>Sequencing</td><td>✅ Handled by job</td><td>❌ MuleSoft must enforce</td></tr><tr><td>Upsert support (product)</td><td>✅ Merge mode native</td><td>❌ GET + POST/PUT per record</td></tr><tr><td>Inventory write</td><td>✅ XML import</td><td>✅ SCAPI Inventory Lists API (<code>PUT</code>/<code>PATCH</code>)</td></tr><tr><td>Negative inventory guard</td><td>✅ Handled by import job</td><td>❌ MuleSoft must validate before call</td></tr><tr><td>Error visibility</td><td>✅ BM log (job-level + record-level)</td><td>✅ Per-call HTTP response</td></tr><tr><td>MuleSoft dev effort</td><td>Low</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>Price sync</td><td>✅ Pricebook XML import</td><td>❌ <strong>No API exists — must use file-based regardless</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Fit for Zimmermann scale</td><td>✅ Recommended</td><td>⚠ Product/inventory supplement only — price always file-based</td></tr></tbody></table><hr/><h2><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"64e36278-09a6-4ab1-9dc9-bbf72738e062\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">10-sync-flow-diagram</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>10. Sync Flow Diagram</h2><blockquote><p><strong>Diagram placeholder</strong></p><p><em>Rovo prompt: Create a swim-lane sequence diagram titled \"MuleSoft → SFCC Catalogue Sync — SCAPI Admin API Pattern (Hybrid)\". Five vertical swim lanes labelled: \"AP21 / NewStore\", \"MuleSoft\", \"SCAPI Admin API\", \"SFCC WebDAV + Import Job\", \"SFCC Catalogue\". Show the following sequence across three colour-coded flows: Product (blue) — MuleSoft acquires AmOAuth2 token → GET existence check → POST create or PUT update master → POST/PUT each variant → PUT category assignment → each SCAPI call returns 200/201 or error; Inventory (orange) — MuleSoft PUT /inventory/v1/.../inventory-lists/{listId}/product-inventory-records/{productId} per variant per inventory list via SCAPI Inventory Lists Admin API; Price (green) — MuleSoft generates pricebook XML zip → PUT to WebDAV → POST SCAPI Jobs Admin API to trigger sfcc-site-archive-import → poll status → archive or fail. Show a clear visual callout on the Price lane: \"No SCAPI Admin API — file-based only\". Show sequencing dependency arrows: master must exist before variant; variant must exist before inventory. Use Zimmermann brand palette — neutral background, clear typography.</em></p></blockquote><hr/><h2><ac:structured-macro ac:macro-id=\"89e9ae12-4de1-4977-af80-10725cc75765\" ac:name=\"anchor\" ac:schema-version=\"1\"><ac:parameter ac:name=\"\">11-open-items</ac:parameter></ac:structured-macro>11. Open Items</h2><table><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Item</th><th>Owner</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Confirm SCAPI Admin API rate limits per environment (sandbox / staging / production) — required to configure MuleSoft Anypoint throttling policy</td><td>Integration Lead / Salesforce TAM</td><td>Open</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Confirm whether SCAPI Products Admin API supports bulk/batch product operations — if available, this significantly reduces call volume</td><td>Integration Lead / SFCC Architect</td><td>Open</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Confirm inventory sync region coverage for EU, EUIntl, HK, ME</td><td>Integration Lead / Platform team</td><td>Open</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Confirm Account Manager OAuth2 client registration and required scopes (<code>sfcc.inventory.availability.rw</code> + product scopes) for MuleSoft across sandbox, staging, and production</td><td>Integration Lead / SFCC Admin</td><td>Open</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Confirm MuleSoft Anypoint MQ strategy for sequencing (master → variant → inventory) — queue-based vs sequential flow</td><td>MuleSoft Architect</td><td>Open</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Confirm with Salesforce TAM whether a SCAPI Admin API for pricebook entry writes is on the roadmap — if released this would allow a fully API-based pattern</td><td>Integration Lead / Salesforce TAM</td><td>Open</td></tr></tbody></table>",
      "format": "storage"
    },
    "emoji": "1f50c",
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

